requirement = "22998.1"
implementation = "Boundary v2 commits the full memory length and a domain-separated binary tree of padded 4096-byte chunks and carries canonical changed chunks relative to validated initial memory, then the preceding boundary of this record. The root-instance engine memory copy is restored from the same committed memory. Replay leaf/node hashing, witness framing and from_captured fuel validation stay unchanged. Profiled calls commit their replay record without also materializing the legacy full-state trace. Two real bootstrap boundaries supply engine metadata, then native execute_step releases each full snapshot after encoding it; the unchanged 64 MiB observer limits apply to each live step and the unchanged profile limits to the entire record."
evidence_memory = "After the Merkle proofs, a bounded count and sorted chunk-index/4096-byte pairs describe pre-memory relative to initialized module memory. OPEN, TRANSITION and TERMINAL restore it and authenticate its root before using it; the native step produces the post root and changes relative to that pre-memory. A changed evidence chunk answers Evidence, including through the ABI-v5 host."
required_admitted_count = 128
admitted_count = "By reference: the executor and sandbox metric lines in the final passing verify row of /out/run/gates.jsonl; each proof asserts exactly 128 admitted host calls."
