before_breakdown = "Middle boundary measured by previous_format_breakdown in repair_22_31_577: boundary prefix 31 bytes; packed arbitration field (4-byte framing), canonical identity 218 bytes including version (plus two 4-byte legacy/engine field frames), legacy execution state (three 32-byte digests, memory root/change section, storage overlay, usage), engine state; frames (4 + sum(16 + operand count)), canonical instruction (4 + instruction bytes), instruction fuel/expansion 16, supplement 48; packed semantic field (4-byte framing), whose canonical host/storage/payment/composition witness sizes are printed separately; trap 1. Exact raw and packed lengths are recorded by reference in the final verify log, measured from the same real middle snapshot before the replacement layout. Memory payload remains 40 + 4100 * changed chunks within the legacy memory field."
after_breakdown = "The final verify log prints the same middle boundary as plain fields: a 32-byte header binding, compact arbitration (legacy and engine lengths), frames/instruction, supplement, each semantic witness and memory section. No compression is used on the production path."
header = "Record constants: identity, execution parameters digest, trace policy, host base/receipt/balance roots and semantic storage baseline. Each compact leaf binds the canonical header digest. Decoder restores omitted legacy identity, overlay and metered usage; producer refuses Binding if record constants disagree."
